    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **Cal Raleigh** emerges as our premier offensive anchor with a 78.02 efficiency score. The combination of a favorable matchup against a struggling lefty in Kay (5.28 xERA) and beneficial wind conditions creates an ideal launchpad for his power profile. Similarly, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Taylor Ward** (71.19) are set to capitalize on high-park-factor environments. **Butler**\u2019s massive +13% dynamic platoon edge against Baz provides the highest upside among our outfielders, while **Ward** remains a top-tier play despite a slightly diluted platoon edge, as his volume in the #2 spot against Civale provides the necessary floor for a high-output evening.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s toughest decision centered on **Wenceel Perez**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 49.88. While he offers some versatility, the combination of a high-ceiling outing from **Gavin Sheets** and the strategic need to prioritize the speed/OBP combination of **Masyn Winn** and **Geraldo Perdomo** pushed **Perez** to the bench. We are proceeding with caution regarding our top-order hitters; specifically, **Will Smith**, **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Gavin Sheets** are currently operating on \"Lineup Pending\" status. While we have baked aggressive assumptions into their projections, any late-scratch or defensive-replacement shuffling by their respective clubs could necessitate a rapid re-evaluation of our utility usage, especially for **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who faces a high-skill arm in Ryan and needs to outperform his currently dampened 56.56 efficiency score to justify his spot.",
